Then, later on, she picks 21 more roses. So, that means she adds 21 roses to her current total. So, the next step is to take the 35 she had left after selling and add 21 to it. Let me calculate that: 35 plus 21. Hmm, 35 plus 20 is 55, and then plus 1 more is 56. So, 35 plus 21 equals 56. Therefore, after selling 15 and then picking 21 more, she should have 56 roses.

